WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:15.650
43. NEAT. The acronym NEAT stands for Not in Education, Employment, or Training. NEAT

2
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:21.810
usually refers to people who have been out of work, school, and training for some time.

3
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:27.130
NEAT people often have negative psychological states. Some of these are causes of their

4
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:33.850
NEAT status, others are results. Many young people become NEAT because they don't have

5
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:41.670
good job qualifications. In this slow economy, competition for jobs is fierce. Because they

6
00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:47.850
think they have poor qualifications, they may lack confidence. Without confidence, they

7
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:54.090
may lose motivation and forget how to even set goals, let alone how to achieve them.

8
00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:59.610
Their NEAT status can pull them into a vicious circle. The longer they are away from a job,

9
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:05.490
the more difficult it is for them to find one and perform in it. According to the Princess

10
00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:11.170
Trust Youth Index of 2010, many NEAT youth feel more negative about the world than their

11
00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:19.050
peers. The 16- to 25-year-old people in the survey were less likely to feel happy or loved

12
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:25.050
most of the time. They were far more likely to agree with statements like, My life has

13
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:30.970
no direction, I do not feel valued by those around me, I have nothing to look forward

14
00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:38.810
to, and even, I have felt suicidal. The obvious solution for NEATs is a better economy and

15
00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:45.530
more jobs. More importantly, we need to create a society where being out of work is not a

16
00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:52.770
source of shame. Life is about more than work. We human beings should remember that our lives

17
00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:59.570
are valuable for a huge variety of reasons. A paycheck shouldn't be the only one.
